Network golden rows N1-N5: the network halves of the design's network
rows. Package unshorten's TestNetworkGolden replays each section over its
loopback test network: production code reaches the listeners by their real
hostnames, with the real dial guard in the dial path. Nothing here is ever
requested from a real host. The offline halves are N1/offline,
N2/offline and N2/offline-categories in positive.txtar.

Each "-- <id> --" section is one case: "key: value" lines, value = rest of
the line verbatim; blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.

  in:          input URL (required, once)
  registry:    entries added to DefaultRegistry, space-separated; "bit.ly"
               is the bit.ly row of the default-registry table, which ships
               unregistered (added with Registry.With)
  generic:     PreviewOnly (default), Follow or Skip
  server:      METHOD URL → STATUS [LOCATION]: the listener for URL's scheme
               and host answers exactly this request (path and query as
               written); any other request to it fails the case
  body:        the text/html body of the previous server: line's response
  listen:      URL: a listener for URL's scheme and host that answers 500 to
               every request; with requests: it shows a host is never
               contacted
  requests:    URL N: the listener for URL's scheme and host received N
               requests in total, after every run of the case
  want:        expected URL under AffiliateKeep, and under AffiliateStrip
               unless want-strip is given
  want-strip:  expected URL under AffiliateStrip
  err:         none (the default), or the sentinel the error wraps besides
               ErrUnresolved (ErrFallback, ErrNoMatch, ...)
  hops: none | hop: <JSON>     Process's Hops in order, under both policies
  hop-keep:, hop-strip:        likewise, under one policy only
  removed: none | removed: <JSON>   Process's Removed in order, both policies
  removed-keep:, removed-strip:     likewise, under one policy only
               (JSON fields as in positive.txtar; listed fields compared,
               the count must match)
  note:        free text

Every case runs Resolve and then Process under AffiliateKeep, then both
again through a WithCleaner(AffiliateStrip) view of the same Resolver.
Every run after the first is served from the cache: no new request, and
Result.Cached when there are hops. Each run also asserts Clean(URL) == URL
and Process(in).URL == Resolve(in).URL, and on an error URL == Clean(in)
and errors.Is(err, ErrUnresolved).
-- N1 --
note: http://t.co: scheme-agnostic match; exactly one HTTPS request, the plain-http listener untouched (DR-F11)
in: http://t.co/abc
server: GET https://t.co/abc → 301 https://example.net/p?utm_source=x
listen: http://t.co
listen: https://example.net
requests: https://t.co 1
requests: http://t.co 0
requests: https://example.net 0
want: https://example.net/p
hop: {"category":"unshortened","rule":"unshorten:t.co","fromHost":"t.co","from":"https://t.co/abc","to":"https://example.net/p?utm_source=x"}
removed: {"part":"query","category":"tracker","name":"utm_source"}
-- N2 --
note: ‡ affiliate interplay (ER-C5): the destination's tag and linkCode kept under Keep (MD-3), stripped under Strip, with the destination's categories after the CatUnshortened hop (MA-2); the destination is never requested
in: https://amzn.to/xyz
server: GET https://amzn.to/xyz → 301 https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0?tag=aff-20&linkCode=ll1&ref_=as_li
listen: https://www.amazon.com
requests: https://amzn.to 1
requests: https://www.amazon.com 0
want: https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0?tag=aff-20&linkCode=ll1
want-strip: https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0
hop: {"category":"unshortened","rule":"unshorten:amazon","fromHost":"amzn.to","from":"https://amzn.to/xyz","to":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0?tag=aff-20&linkCode=ll1&ref_=as_li"}
removed-keep: {"part":"query","category":"tracker","name":"ref_"}
removed-strip: {"part":"query","category":"affiliate","name":"tag","network":"Amazon Associates","id":"aff-20"}
removed-strip: {"part":"query","category":"affiliate","name":"linkCode","network":"Amazon Associates","id":""}
removed-strip: {"part":"query","category":"tracker","name":"ref_"}
-- N3 --
note: per-entry fallback: amzn.to's answer is Amazon's homepage, so the input is returned with ErrFallback; also from the cache
in: https://amzn.to/xyz
server: GET https://amzn.to/xyz → 301 https://www.amazon.com/
listen: https://www.amazon.com
requests: https://amzn.to 1
requests: https://www.amazon.com 0
want: https://amzn.to/xyz
err: ErrFallback
hops: none
removed: none
-- N4 --
note: stop at the first host that is not allowlisted: returned, never requested. The design's row uses evil.example; .example has no ICANN site, so the approved next-URL validation (rawurl.ParseTarget, Q4) would make that ErrBadTarget, and this row uses evil.example.net to keep pinning the stop
in: https://t.co/abc
server: GET https://t.co/abc → 301 https://evil.example.net/x
listen: https://evil.example.net
requests: https://t.co 1
requests: https://evil.example.net 0
want: https://evil.example.net/x
hop: {"category":"unshortened","rule":"unshorten:t.co","fromHost":"t.co","from":"https://t.co/abc","to":"https://evil.example.net/x"}
removed: none
-- N5 --
note: no-click preview first: under PreviewOnly bit.ly is fetched only as GET /abc+ and the destination comes from the info page. bit.ly ships unregistered (Q18), so the row adds the entry with Registry.With; TestNetworkGoldenN5NoMatch pins the ErrNoMatch half
in: https://bit.ly/abc
registry: bit.ly
server: GET https://bit.ly/abc+ → 200
body: <div class="bitlink--destination-text"><ul><li><a class="item-detail--url" href="https://example.net/dest?utm_source=bitly" title="https://example.net/dest?utm_source=bitly" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://example.net/dest?utm_source=bitly</a></li></ul></div>
listen: https://example.net
requests: https://bit.ly 1
requests: https://example.net 0
want: https://example.net/dest
hop: {"category":"unshortened","rule":"unshorten:bit.ly","fromHost":"bit.ly","from":"https://bit.ly/abc","to":"https://example.net/dest?utm_source=bitly"}
removed: {"part":"query","category":"tracker","name":"utm_source"}
